{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The source is the 1982 Intellivision game later called *Cloudy Mountain*. Its defining ideas are scarce arrows, hidden cave routes, sound clues, ricochets, and tools that open the overworld. I’m centering the plan on those. I’m also checking standalone multiplayer separately: the AI Hub client does not provide room discovery outside the Hub.\n"}}
